# musing — project context

**Start here**: **`AGENTS.md`** — install/configure/run/test commands, constraints, and
definition of done, shared with Claude Code and any other agent. This rule stays as the
Cursor-native always-apply entry point for stack/layout details; keep the two in sync in
spirit, don't duplicate long content here.

## Stack

Vite 8, React 19, TypeScript, React Router 8 (`react-router` — do not use `react-router-dom`); TipTap 3 (one document per page via `PageDocumentEditor` — see `.cursor/skills/editor-tiptap/`). Optional Supabase.

## `src/` (where to look)

Routes: `main.tsx`, `App.tsx` (import routing APIs from `react-router`). Workspace: `context/WorkspaceContext.tsx`, `useWorkspace.ts`, `lib/workspaceStorage.ts`. Editor: `Editor.tsx`, `PageDocumentEditor.tsx`, `SlashMenu.tsx`, `PagePickerMenu.tsx`. Extensions: `extensions/` (e.g. `wikiLink.ts`). Slash/commands: `lib/slashMenuOptions.ts`, `lib/blockEditorCommands.ts`. Types: `types/block.ts`, `types/page.ts`. Supabase: `lib/supabaseClient.ts`, `lib/supabaseWorkspace.ts` (not the `supabase/` SQL folder).

## Vite: `@tiptap/pm/*` aliases

Rolldown won’t resolve `@tiptap/pm/*` subpaths — keep the full `resolve.alias` map in `vite.config.ts` → `prosemirror-*`. New PM subpath? Add the alias.

## Pages / `BASE_URL`

`pagesBase()` + optional `VITE_BASE_PATH` set Vite `base` → `import.meta.env.BASE_URL`. `BrowserRouter` `basename` in `main.tsx` strips a trailing slash. Any app URL (wiki links, exports) must use `BASE_URL`, not assume `/` at the host root.

## Supabase (optional)

Schema/RLS: `supabase/schema.sql`. Env: `VITE_SUPABASE_*` in `.env.local`; same names as GitHub **repository secrets** for deploy/keepalive (README). No Supabase → localStorage only; don’t assume DB in all paths.

## AI second-brain layer (optional)

`service/` (`musing-ai-service`) — separate Node/TS backend, own toolchain, deployed to Cloud Run, called cross-origin from `src/lib/aiClient.ts`. See `.cursor/rules/ai-service.mdc` for the full picture; don’t assume it’s configured or reachable (`isAiServiceConfigured()` gates every FE code path).

## Scoped rules and skills

- **Rules** (auto when matching files are open): `readme`, `frontend-testing`, `editor-tiptap`, `workspace-supabase`, `ai-service` under `.cursor/rules/`.
- **Skills** (read `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` when the task fits):
